    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im a freelance designer and im trying to organize my quickbooks for the year. i just bought a really expensive ergonomic office chair for my home studio. do i categorize that as a business expense or is it a personal draw? i want to make sure i dont mess up my deductions.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Great question! In this case, since you purchased the ergonomic office chair for use in your home studio where you work as a freelancer, you can classify it as a business expense. Make sure to keep all records and receipts that can verify it was bought for business purposes. Keeping your business and personal expenses well-differentiated on your QuickBooks account is essential for accurate tax deductions.",
      "source": "target",
