    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i also have a bunch of smaller stuff, like random software subs and some hardware. what's the rule for stuff that costs under $250? i feel like i'm constantly losing track of small receipts and it's making my books a mess.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For expenses under $250, small-ticket items like software subscriptions and certain hardware, you still need to track them. Even though there's a de minimis rule that allows you to primarily use tax software for reporting expenses below a certain threshold, maintaining personal records is essential in case of an audit. For the software you'll get the most benefit from specific accounting software like QuickBooks Automatic Data Capture (ADC) or other apps like Receipt Bank which can scan and categorize those small expenses automatically. These tools can greatly help you maintain clear and organized records.",
      "source": "target",
